 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Keep the fridge as cold as possible, around three degrees Celsius. A freezer bag works too, but keep it in the kitchen so it's easy to see. They melt on the road, and condensation makes the box wet. Pack them flat or in small box next to the fridge. Leave the door open on Sunday you' leaving, so it' not too cold when you get there. And pack a spare blanket in case the oil from the food melts the blanket too. Teach him to leave it on Saturday so the food stays fresh. You could even leave a small pot of water boiling on the stove.",
